 ## Background
-The concept emerged as a solution to "floaters" and geometric inaccuracies common in early neural radiance fields (NeRF) [G]. While early NeRFs optimized density and color independently, later works recognized that explicit geometric priors (like SDFs) could regularize the density field [G]. The specific formulations of SRDF-SDF consistency and Density Consistency Loss appear in recent literature (circa 2023) focusing on fine-detail reconstruction and multi-view consistency . The Geometry Bias Loss is specifically associated with methods that combine volume rendering with SDF-based surface extraction, aiming to align the probabilistic surface from rendering with the deterministic surface from the SDF .
